```
+----------------------+
|          E           |
|                      |
|      *               |
|                      |
|   P                  |
|                 E    |
+----------------------+

P = player
E = enemy
* = projectile
```

First a couple of things
ENTITY = ID
Component = Entity Data
Systems = ACTS on ENTITY DATA 

this will all be in 2D space using stationary objects

Factory constructs/configures entities <---> Registry creates ENTITY IDs and OWNS COMPONENT STORAGE <------> Systems hold/use non-owning Registry references 

THE REGISTRY OWNS ENTITY LIFECYCLE AND COMPONENT STORAGE.
THE FACTORY ASKS THE REGISTRY TO CREATE AN ENTITY ID, THEN ATTACHES THE APPROPRIATE COMPONENTS TO THAT ID

Generating component storage through a template class - ensuring type safety at compile time

Okay so in this situation it looks like we have 4 entities 
(1) target/enemy (2) projectile (3) weapon (4) player

Components: (1) target (2) projectile (3) lifetime (4) transform/position (5) weapon (6) velocity (7) health

Systems would include (1) movement (position, velocity) (2) lifetime (3) weapon system 

Simulated step: 60Hz 

In the entity factory:
Target{target, lifetime, position}
Project{projectile, lifetime, velocity, position}
Weapon{weapon, position}
Player{lifetime, position}


Linking Entity ID to components 
Example: 
Target/Enemy uint32_t = ID1
std::vector<Target> [ID1 target data, ]
std::vector<Projectile> [ ]
std::vector<Lifetime> [ ID1 lifetime data , ]
std::vector<Position> [ ID1 position data ]
std::vector<Weapon> [ ]
std::vector<Velocity> [ ]
std::vector<Health> [ ]


Developing the Templated class 
namespace engine {

    template <typename T> 
    class ComponentStorage{
        public:

        private:
            std::vector<T> components_;
            std::vector<Entity> entities_;
            std::unordered_map<Entity, std::size_t> entityToIndex_;
    };
}

Suppose we are working on ComponentStorage<Position> and the following entites have these positions:
Entity 1 -> Position{2, 3}
Entity 2 -> Position{8, 1}
Entity 3 -> Position{5, 9}

The three containers would then look like: 
Component Data 
components_ = {
    Position{2, 3},  // index 0
    Position{8, 1},  // index 1
    Position{5, 9}   // index 2
}

entites_ = {
    Entity{1},   // index 0
    Entity{4},   // index 1
    Entity{7}    // index 2
};

So the unordered map would conceptually look like: 
entityToIndex_ = {
    {Entity{1}, 0},
    {Entity{4}, 1},
    {Entity{7}, 2}
};